Language English

Book OpenGate Ordered No Keep Looped
	Triggered By @InteractAltar

	Mark Step3Repeat Read

    Page Step1Prolog
        Text """
			Matthias stands at the alter, arms raised, speaking
			a language you don't understand. You can see on the altar the
			various tools and materials needed for the ritual.
			
			The boy is chained to the floor, crying and quietly begging his
			father to stop. A cowering woman is chained near Matthias at the
			altar.
			
			The woman is screaming now and something is happening to her body.
			Matthias continues speaking, but this time the waves of power seem
			to be coming from the air and into him.
			
            If you have the {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the {c:QItemElderSign}, you can
			begin to disrupt the ritual.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this task and only
            while standing at the altar in the same space as Matthias.
        
            Are you ready?
        """

		If firstRitual >= firstRitualWoman Then Text """
			Matthias stands at the alter, arms raised, speaking
			a language you don't understand. You can see on the altar the
			various tools and materials needed for the ritual.
			
			The boy is chained to the floor, crying and quietly begging his
			father to stop. A woman lies dead at his feet, her face locked in a
			scream that will never end.
			
            If you have the {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the
			{c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the {c:QItemElderSign}, you can
			begin to disrupt the ritual.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this task and only
            while standing at the altar in the same space as Matthias.
        
            Are you ready?
        """

        Button 1 "Speak the words"
		Button 2 "Not Yet"

		If selection = 1 And firstRitual >= firstRitualWoman Then Goto Step1
		If selection = 1 Then Goto Woman
		Exit
	End Page Step1Prolog
	
	Page Woman
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenDeadWoman
		
		Text """
			As you step closer, Matthias lowers then flings his arms upward.
			The woman screams, gasps for air, then screams again. The power you
			felt before comes in waves, but this time is feels like it is 
			going into Matthias. The woman abruptly stops screaming, goes rigid,
			the goes limp. A momentary glow surrounds Matthias and he lowers his
			arms long enough to flip to a different page in the book he has on
			the altar. The woman is dead.
			
			Sarah whispers, <<Matthias has recharged himself. He is at
			the final stage. He is ready to open the gate.>>
		"""
		
		Remove TokenLiveWoman
		
		Goto Step1
	End Page Woman
	
	Page step1
		firstRitual = 0
		mainRitual = mainRitualStarted
		
        Text """
			You look closer at the altar. You notice that
			Matthias does not have an {c:QItemElderSign}. That
			means he will need blood to keep the gate open. You must stop him
			before he uses you to supply it.
			
			You think back to the counter-spell you memorized earlier. You hold
			the {c:QItemRitualKnife} and chalice above your head and speak the
			words. Matthias snaps his head toward you, as though seeing
			you for the first time. Your eyes lock and you see a 
			determined but haunted look in his eyes.
			
			He looks back at the altar and tries to start again. Nothing comes
			out of his mouth and he looks back at you.
			
			This step is complete.
        """
    End Page Step1

    Page Step2
        Prolog """
            Your cousin lowers his eyes to the dagger he holds. While no
			sound comes out, you see him moving his lips.
        """

        Button "Stab Matthias first"

        Text """
			You choose your moment and lunge at him with your knife. He deftly
			steps to the left and your knife glances off of his
			robe, doing no damage.
			
			You think you can turn and make a more direct hit. Test {agility}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        """
		
		// even if we pass, we fail
        Test Quota 10 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step2

    Page Step3
        Prolog """
			He steps away again and you stumble, bumping into him and knocking
			the {c:QItemRitualDagger} from his hand. It clatters onto the altar
			and you step back.
        """

		Button "Speak the words"

        Text """
			Matthias grabs the knife and begins speaking the
			incantation again, his voice booming with power. The knife suddenly
			glows and then, lightly, begins pulsing.
			
			You speak the words again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        """

        // even if we pass, we fail
		Test Quota 4 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step3

    Page Step3Fail
        Text """
            You fumble the words and nothing happens. Matthias
			ignores you and slides the blade across his palm.
        
            Suffer 2 Horror ({will} negates).
			
			<<You must stop him,>> Sarah stammers.
        """

        Mark Step3Repeat Unread
    End Page Step3Fail

	Page Step3Repeat
		Prolog """
			Surprised that the spell didn't work, you raise your arms again.
		"""
		
		Button "Speak the words"
		
		Text """
			You begin speaking, hoping to block his voice again. Test {will}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
		"""
		
		Test Quota 4 Set passOpenGateStep3
		If passOpenGateStep3 Then Goto Step4
	End Page Step3Repeat

	Page Step3RepeatFail
	
		Text """
			Matthias seems unfazed as blood wells up from the 
			cut in his palm. You look at the dagger and chalice raised in your
			hands and wonder why nothing is happening. You take a deep breath,
			determined to stop this madness.
		"""

		Mark Unread
		Mark Step3Repeat Unread
	End Page Step3RepeatFail

    Page Step4
		Mark Step3RepeatFail Read
		
        Prolog """
            Matthias squeezes blood from his fist into the
			chalice, speaking in that same unknown language. As he does, you can
			feel your spell take hold... he loses his voice again.
        """

        Button "Make your move"

        Text """
			With Matthias both frustrated and distracted, you reach
			out to grab the skull. If only you can reach it before he... does
			something.
			
			Test {agility}.
			
			For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
       """
   
       // even if we pass, we fail
	   Test Quota 10 Set passWhoCares
    End Page Step4

	Page Step4Fail
		Text """
			Matthias swings his arm at you, dagger flashing in the low
			light. It catches your arm, causing you to drop your dagger.
			
			Drop {c:QItemRitualKnife}. Take 2 {damage} ({agility} negates).
			
			Matthias squeezes more of his blood into the chalice, 
			causing it to... change in a way you cannot describe. It somehow
			feels powerful, like the knife he is wielding.
		"""
	End Page Step4Fail
	
    Page KillHim
		Prolog """
			You stop for a moment to think. You need to decide what to do next
			and you need to decide quickly.
			
			Sarah quavers, <<You have do something. He is nearly done casting.
			Please.>>
		"""
		Button "Make your decision"
		
        Text """
            The futility of trying to stop your uncle from completing this
			ritual sinks in. You're going to have to kill him.
			
			Meanwhile, across the room, your friends are fighting for their 
			lives against what seems to be a never-ending stream of local
			townsfolk in cult robes.
			
			Your cousin still concentrates on the his casting.
        """
	
		// we need to replace unattackable monster with one we can attack
		
		Call Event SpawnAltarMatthiasOpenGate
		
		// does this make the DVM go away? (???)
		Remove QItemDvm
    End Page KillHim
	
	Epilog
		Not Visible
		
		No Prolog
		No Text
	End Epilog
	
	Page SarahTransports
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @CompleteRequirement If goal = goalOpenGate And foundKnife And foundDvm And foundElderSign And foundDungeonCell And exploredCryptViaChapel And exploredDungeonCaveViaBasement
		
		Text """
			Sarah smiles for the first time and says out load, <<That's it! Now
			we know what is going on, where it's happening, and what to do about
			it. I think I can take us where we need to be.>>
			
			Sarah seems to grow, getting more transparent. Suddenly, the world
			shifts and you are... somewhere else. And disoriented. There is
			noise and light and someone yelling. Folks are rushing by. It all
			seems far away.>>
		"""
		
		If firstRitual < firstRitualWoman Call MythosFirstRitualOpenGate.Woman
		
		firstRitual = false
		Trigger @ExploreAltar
		Goto Init
	End Page SarahTransports
End Book OpenGate

Book MatthiasOpenGateActivation Ordered No Keep
	Page First
		Text """
			Matthias picks up the chalice, a drop of blood still dripping down
			its inside surface. He examines it carefully, then, seemingly
			satisfied, he sets it back onto altar. He raises his other arm,
			dagger still in his hand. After steadying the chalice, he reaches
			over and flips a page in his book. He glances down, then looks to
			the boy and begins speaking. As he does, you are briefly stunned by
			the wave of energy that radiates from him.
			
			Each investigator takes 1 facedown damage ({agility} negates).
			
			Each cultist takes 1 damage.
		"""
	End Page First

	Page Second
		Text """
			Matthias begins speaking again, power radiating from him like it
			did before. His is intent on his son or starts to move. As you watch
			the boy begins to hover, being slowly pulled up like his on a
			string. You hear the chain clank when it slips. 
			
			Sarah is panicking, look back and forth between her uncle and her
			cousin. <<Do something,>> she yells. <<Do something now!>>
			
			Matthias doesn't notice, all of his attention focused on the words
			he's speaking and the boy who is their target.
		"""
	End Page Second
	
	Page Third
		Text """
			The boy screams as a glow begins to form around him. He stops rising
			as the chain binding him to the floor is pulled taut. He is still
			screaming. At the altar, Matthias is still casting the spell, all 
			his attention focused, obvious to any of the other people in the
			small room.
			
			Sarah shrieks at Matthias, <<Stop! Please stop!>>
			
			With a final flourish of his knife, Matthias completes the spell.
			A bolt strikes from the tip of the blade to the boys chest. When it
			hits, the boy stops screaming and goes rigid. 
			
			Everyone stops and turns to watch, the room going completely silent
			for a moment. Then, with a roar, the boy... changes. He is suddenly
			something more. Something surging and abyssal, but unstable. The
			gate is open and, somehow, the boy <i>is</i> the gate.
			
			Sarah cries out in anguish.
			
			The gate sputters.
		End Text
		
		gateOpen = true
	End Page Third
	
	Page Fourth
		Text """
			This fight is exhausting you and, for a moment, you stop to catch
			your breath.
			
			As you do, Matthias flip forward many pages in the book, smiling
			when he finds what he is looking for. He raises his arms and begins
			speaking again. His own blood still drips from the dagger, landing
			on the altar. You can feel it in the air as each drop hits.

			Sarah yells, <<He's starting the summoning. The Ancient One has 
			heard his call. We are running out of time.>>
			
			Another cultist enters the room, steps toward the gate, raises a
			dagger, and slits his own throat. When blood touches the boy's 
			chain, the gate calms and becomes more stable. It still pops, but 
			not as strongly now.
		"""
		
		summoning = true
	End Page Fourth
	
	Page Fifth
		Text """
			Matthias continues to speak, his voice booming in the chamber. He
			punctuates each sentence by stabbing the air with his dagger.
			Suddenly, stops and just watches the gate as a lone tentacle
			pokes through.
			
			The investigation is over.
		"""
		
		lose = true
		Trigger @GameOver
	End Page Fifth
	
End Book MatthiasOpenGateActivation
